<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Corwill half yr shr rises, no div.</title>
<headline>Corwill half yr shr rises, no div.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-12-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended Sept 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     8.6	   vs 6.5</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 none	  vs 9.0</p>
<p>    After tax income	0.16	  vs 0.12</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   0.17	  vs 0.12</p>
<p>    Tax			 none	  vs none</p>
<p>    Expenses		  0.03	  vs 0.04</p>
<p>    Turnover		  0.20	  vs 0.16</p>
<p>Full name: Corwill Investments Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Corwill's sole investment remains its holding of 557,604 stock units and 2.04 million preferred shares in Willoughby's Consolidated Plc, directors said.</p>
<p>They said the proposed nine cent dividend was not approved by shareholders and the effect of this was to increase net asset value per share to 268 cents from 259 before.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
